# Probes the Python front end (unisa/front, the control group `python3 -m unisa fat`
# drives) does not handle yet, one per line: <probe> <why>.  Same contract as
# tests/c99.knownfail: a listed probe may fail here; a listed probe that starts
# passing on both slices FAILS the suite -- close it by deleting its line.  The C
# reference and the shipped product are held to these by difftest/closure; this
# is the Python route's debt (FX-6 control group, not on the shipping path).
# Opened 2026-09-30 (0.0.13).
fb12-19-function-typedef Python parser: function typedef (`typedef int fn(int); fn twice;`) is rejected
fb12-20-comma-in-conditional-middle Python parser: comma in the middle operand of ?:
fb12-31-unused-static-refs-undefined Python front end: an unreferenced static's call to an undefined function is still reported
n17-line Python preprocessor: no __LINE__
n17-file Python preprocessor: no __FILE__
n17-linedir R14-3 P2 the Python front end has no #line (the C reference and the network do)
n17-line-alone R14-3 P2 the Python front end has no __LINE__
n17-linedir-macro R14-3 P2 the Python front end has no #line
a_parenfn 0.0.21 the Python front end treats T (name)(args) as a variable (the C reference and cc agree)
a_tdlate 0.0.21 the Python front end lacks __builtin_offsetof, comma controls and late-completed typedef sizes
a_offsetof 0.0.23 the Python front end lacks offsetof/__builtin_offsetof (the C reference prints 8 48 56 / 56, matching cc)
